# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit .env.
# Application role: RLS enforced, cannot bypass (deploy/dev/init.sql creates it).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://rocky_app_dev:rocky-dev-only@127.0.0.1:54329/rocky
# Worker login (P3-3, ADR 0009): a member of rocky_app and rocky_worker. Only the worker creates
# orgs, claims webhook inbox rows and erases orgs. `pnpm seed` creates this dev role on an
# existing volume; new volumes get it from deploy/dev/init.sql. Never use it as DATABASE_URL:
# the server starts only on a plain rocky_app login (not the worker's, not the owner's or the
# migrator's, not a superuser; a platform-issued owner URL such as `fly postgres attach` gives is
# refused too).
WORKER_DATABASE_URL=postgres://rocky_worker_dev:rocky-dev-only@127.0.0.1:54329/rocky
# Table owner: runs migrations (`pnpm db:migrate`). Never used by the server or worker.
DATABASE_ADMIN_URL=postgres://rocky:rocky-dev-only@127.0.0.1:54329/rocky
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=4310
LOG_LEVEL=info
# Local key-encryption keys for envelope encryption (ADR-0006): `id=<base64 32 bytes>` entries,
# comma-separated. `pnpm dev` generates a dev key into .env on first run. Rotation: add the new
# key, set ROCKY_KEK_CURRENT to its id, re-wrap, then remove the old one.
# ROCKY_KEK_KEYS=dev=<generated>
# ROCKY_KEK_CURRENT=dev
# GitHub webhook secret (P3-2, ADR 0007): at least 32 characters, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Required in production (NODE_ENV=production, or FLY_APP_NAME set on Fly.io): the server
# refuses to boot without it; unset in
# development disables POST /webhooks/github.
# GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Webhook inbox retention / dedup window in days (default 30, minimum 7), applied by db:migrate.
# RETENTION_WEBHOOK_DELIVERIES_DAYS=30
# GitHub App manifest setup (P3-1, ADR 0008; runbook docs/runbooks/h3-create-github-app.md).
# `true` opens one-time setup routes (printed URL in the terminal); refused in production and
# ignored once GITHUB_APP_ID is set or the credentials file exists. Remove after creating the app.
# GITHUB_APP_SETUP=true
# https URL GitHub delivers webhooks to (local dev: a smee.io channel). Defaults to
# <ROCKY_PUBLIC_URL>/webhooks/github when ROCKY_PUBLIC_URL is https.
# GITHUB_APP_WEBHOOK_URL=https://smee.io/<channel>
# Where Rocky is reached (https, or http on 127.0.0.1/localhost). Default http://HOST:PORT.
# ROCKY_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4310
# GITHUB_APP_NAME=Rocky Reviews
# The app's homepage on GitHub (https; default ROCKY_PUBLIC_URL), e.g. the repository URL.
# GITHUB_APP_HOMEPAGE_URL=
# Absolute path, written once with mode 0600 (default ~/.rocky/github-app.env).
# GITHUB_APP_CREDENTIALS_FILE=
# GitHub Enterprise Server (https only): GITHUB_URL=https://ghe.example.com (API defaults to /api/v3)
# GITHUB_URL=
# GITHUB_API_URL=
# App credentials (from the credentials file; keep the real values in a secret manager).
# The worker needs GITHUB_APP_ID and GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY to verify installation events with
# GitHub (P3-3): required in production; without them in development installation events wait
# in the inbox. The key must be an RSA PEM of at least 2048 bits (multi-line, or with \n).
# GITHUB_APP_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=   (the PEM, multi-line, inside single quotes, as the credentials file has it)
# LLM roles (P4-1, ADR 0012). Nothing set: every completion role on the Anthropic API with the
# defaults (triage claude-haiku-5-5/low, review claude-opus-5-5/high, graph and ask
# claude-sonnet-5-5/medium) and embeddings off. Empty counts as unset; an unknown ROCKY_LLM_*
# variable is refused. Keys are never set here by value: *_API_KEY_ENV names the variable
# holding the key.
# Providers: anthropic, bedrock, vertex, foundry, openai-compatible. Moves every role:
# ROCKY_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Per role (TRIAGE, REVIEW, GRAPH, ASK): provider, model, effort (low|medium|high|xhigh|max,
# as far as the provider and model support it). On openai-compatible the model is required.
# ROCKY_LLM_REVIEW_PROVIDER=
# ROCKY_LLM_REVIEW_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# ROCKY_LLM_REVIEW_EFFORT=high
# Bedrock, Vertex and Foundry only: the literal id to send, e.g. a Bedrock inference profile
# (eu.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5) or ARN, a Vertex dated id (no / or :), a Foundry deployment
# name (letters, digits, . _ -). MODEL stays the canonical id used to validate effort. Unset, the
# adapter sends anthropic.<model> on Bedrock and the canonical id elsewhere (P4-2, ADR 0013).
# ROCKY_LLM_REVIEW_PLATFORM_MODEL=
# Embeddings: off until all three are set (no default model; ADR 0012 §6). Today only
# openai-compatible serves embeddings.
# ROCKY_LLM_EMBED_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
# ROCKY_LLM_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
# ROCKY_LLM_EMBED_DIMENSIONS=768
# Anthropic API: the key's variable (default ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) and an optional gateway URL
# (https only). Refusals fall back server-side (fallbacks: "default") on the models that take it;
# FALLBACKS=off turns that off, e.g. for a gateway that rejects the beta.
# These SDK variables are overridden, because Rocky sets each option explicitly:
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_LOG, ANTHROPIC_OPEN_TELEMETRY*, and the
# platform ones (ANTHROPIC_*_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID, CLOUD_ML_REGION,
# ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_*). These are refused (the worker will not start while they are set):
# ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS (could replace the auth headers) and, with Vertex,
# GOOGLE_SDK_NODE_LOGGING (logs access tokens). Others are not read by Rocky's clients, and
# NODE_DEBUG / HTTPS_PROXY stay operator choices (ADR 0013, residual risks).
# ROCKY_LLM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_ENV=ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# ROCKY_LLM_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# ROCKY_LLM_ANTHROPIC_FALLBACKS=on
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Amazon Bedrock, Messages API (Mantle) endpoint: credentials from the AWS default chain, or
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK; region falls back to AWS_REGION, then AWS_DEFAULT_REGION. Opus 4.6,
# Opus 4.5 and Sonnet 4.6 are not served there and are refused.
# ROCKY_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1
# Google Vertex AI (application default credentials):
# ROCKY_LLM_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=
# ROCKY_LLM_VERTEX_REGION=global
# Microsoft Foundry: the resource and the key's variable (default ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_API_KEY).
# ROCKY_LLM_FOUNDRY_RESOURCE=
# ROCKY_LLM_FOUNDRY_API_KEY_ENV=ANTHROPIC_FOUNDRY_API_KEY
# OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, vLLM): base URL and, if it needs one, the key's variable.
# With a key the URL must be https (http only on 127.0.0.1, localhost or [::1]).
# ROCKY_LLM_OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# ROCKY_LLM_OPENAI_API_KEY_ENV=
# Analysis queue lane (P4-6, ADR 0017). The per-PR token limit: an analysis whose estimate (the
# diff after rules pre-triage, noise and unchanged files excluded, plus a fixed overhead per call
# and stage) is above it waits for "Analyze anyway"; no model is called. How many analyses this
# worker runs at once, and how many one org runs at once across every worker.
# ROCKY_ANALYSIS_TOKEN_LIMIT=150000
# ROCKY_ANALYSIS_CONCURRENCY=4
# ROCKY_ANALYSIS_ORG_CONCURRENCY=2
# Automatic analysis: off by default, so nothing is analysed (and nothing spends) until it is on.
# When on, every new head of an open pull request that a webhook reports is queued and analysed.
# ROCKY_ANALYSIS_AUTO=off
